        "x1": 0.4902676056338028,
        "y1": 0.7420896551724139
      },
      "text": ";",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.0801605633802817,
        "y0": 0.7431189655172414,
        "x1": 0.4886450704225352,
        "y1": 0.7702758620689655
      },
      "text": "Lavelugged, Northumb. HoUoway has lapeared in use in Sussex and Hants.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5096985915492958,
        "y0": 0.7436293103448276,
        "x1": 0.8072563380281691,
        "y1": 0.7586396551724137
      },
      "text": "LAWED. Ignorant. See Laird.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5088901408450704,
        "y0": 0.7575344827586207,
        "x1": 0.8436957746478874,
        "y1": 0.7719862068965517
      },
      "text": "LAWES. The same as Kaims, q. v.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5088901408450704,
        "y0": 0.7706,
        "x1": 0.8206169014084508,
        "y1": 0.7851396551724138
      },
      "text": "LAWESTE. The lowest. North.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.05829859154929578,
        "y0": 0.7707603448275862,
        "x1": 0.48986760563380277,
        "y1": 0.7847655172413793
      },
      "text": "LAVEER. To work a ship against the wind.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.05870140845070422,
        "y0": 0.7843551724137932,
        "x1": 0.4902647887323944,
        "y1": 0.8114672413793104
      },
      "text": "An old sea term. LAVELL. The flap that covers the top of the",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5291323943661972,
        "y0": 0.7849241379310345,
        "x1": 0.8906619718309859,
        "y1": 0.7958258620689656
      },
      "text": "Lenges all at laysere, and lokes one the wallys",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5299408450704225,
        "y0": 0.7973517241379311,
        "x1": 0.894712676056338,
        "y1": 0.8083327586206897
      },
      "text": "Whare they ware latveate the ledes to assaille.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6720422535211267,
        "y0": 0.8080724137931035,
        "x1": 0.9404563380281691,
        "y1": 0.8191310344827586
      },
      "text": "Morte Arthure, MS. Lincoln, f. 79»",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.0801605633802817,
        "y0": 0.8115689655172413,
        "x1": 0.3671971830985915,
        "y1": 0.8240086206896552
      },
      "text": "windpipe. Still used in Devon.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5084845070422536,
        "y0": 0.8197896551724138,
        "x1": 0.8857915492957747,
        "y1": 0.8343689655172414
      },
      "text": "LAWFUL-CASE. An interj. of surprize.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.059107042253521126,
        "y0": 0.8237396551724138,
        "x1": 0.48986197183098595,
        "y1": 0.8772189655172414
      },
      "text": "LAVENDER. To lay in lavender, to pawn. This is a very common phrase in old plays. \" To lay to pawne, as we say to lay in lavander,\" Florio, p. 27.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5088901408450704,
        "y0": 0.8328068965517241,
        "x1": 0.7760873239436621,
        "y1": 0.8483068965517242
      },
      "text": "LAWGHE. Low. Hampole.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5088901408450704,
        "y0": 0.8471396551724137,
        "x1": 0.828718309859155,
        "y1": 0.8613913793103448
      },
      "text": "LAWING. (1) Going to law. IJnc.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5088901408450704,
        "y0": 0.8615189655172414,
        "x1": 0.9400450704225353,
        "y1": 0.8755810344827586
      },
      "text": "(2) Lawing of dogs, i. e. cutting out the balls,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5303464788732394,
        "y0": 0.876248275862069,
        "x1": 0.805650704225352,
        "y1": 0.8873465517241379
      },
      "text": "or three claws of the fore-feet.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.05870140845070422,
        "y0": 0.8764137931034482,
        "x1": 0.38622253521126765,
        "y1": 0.8912706896551724
      },
      "text": "LAVENDREY. Washing. (A.-N.)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5092957746478873,
        "y0": 0.8866896551724138,
        "x1": 0.8736478873239436,
        "y1": 0.9013931034482758
      },
      "text": "LAWLESS-MAN. An outlaw. {A.-S.)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.059512676056338025,
        "y0": 0.89085,
        "x1": 0.3935154929577465,
        "y1": 0.904648275862069
      },
      "text": "LAVER. (1) The remainder. North.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5092957746478873,
        "y0": 0.90035,
        "x1": 0.9404535211267605,
        "y1": 0.9287793103448276
      },
      "text": "LAWN. The same as Launde, q. v. LAWNDER. The sliding iron in the fore-part",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.05991830985915493,
        "y0": 0.9034551724137931,
        "x1": 0.48986197183098595,
        "y1": 0.9437517241379311
      },
      "text": "(2) A cistern, trough, or conduit, to wash in. \" Laver to washe at, lavoyr\" Palsgrave. Also, a basin. See Florio, p. 89 ;",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
